{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q421177","formula":"C₁₀H₁₂N₂O","hill":"C10H12N2O","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":10.0,"H":12.0,"N":2.0,"O":1.0},"names":{"en":"Cotinine","ru":"Котинин"},"descriptions":{"en":"Cotinine is an alkaloid found in tobacco and is also the predominant metabolite of nicotine, typically used as a biomarker for exposure to tobacco smoke. Cotinine is currently being studied as a treatment for depression, post-traumatic stress disorder (PTSD), schizophrenia, Alzheimer's disease and Parkinson's disease. Cotinine was developed as an antidepressant as a fumaric acid salt, cotinine fumarate, to be sold under the brand name Scotine, but it was never marketed.","ru":"Котини́н — алкалоид, обнаруженный в табаке и, кроме того, являющийся метаболитом никотина. Слово «котинин» представляет собой анаграмму слова «никотин». Используется как биомаркер воздействия табачного дыма, а также продаётся как антидепрессант под маркой «Scotine»."},"fame":21,"pubchemCid":854019,"mass":176.21,"charge":0,"smiles":"CN1[C@@H](CCC1=O)C2=CN=CC=C2","inchikey":"UIKROCXWUNQSPJ-VIFPVBQESA-N","iupac":"(5S)-1-methyl-5-pyridin-3-ylpyrrolidin-2-one","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"854019","atoms":25,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":3.363,"y":-0.945,"z":-0.628,"el":"O"},{"x":1.545,"y":-0.271,"z":0.708,"el":"N"},{"x":-2.212,"y":-1.24,"z":-0.976,"el":"N"},{"x":0.533,"y":0.774,"z":0.688,"el":"C"},{"x":1.123,"y":1.794,"z":-0.284,"el":"C"},{"x":2.006,"y":0.972,"z":-1.22,"el":"C"},{"x":2.431,"y":-0.199,"z":-0.366,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.849,"y":0.305,"z":0.28,"el":"C"},{"x":1.596,"y":-1.268,"z":1.76,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.985,"y":0.947,"z":0.75,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.01,"y":-0.772,"z":-0.572,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.24,"y":0.496,"z":0.357,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.299,"y":-0.592,"z":-0.499,"e